modplayjs — NOTICE
==================

This project contains code ported from the following reference projects.
The ports mirror the structure and behavior of the originals; the original
copyrights and licenses remain in force for that material. Each published
package carries a NOTICE.md covering only the sources that package
contains; this file lists every source used across the project.

1. OpenMPT — BSD-3-Clause
   Copyright (C) 2004-2026, OpenMPT Project Developers and Contributors
   Copyright (C) 1997-2003, Olivier Lapicque (original ModPlug Tracker)
   Ported from: soundlib (MODTools.cpp, InstrumentSynth.cpp/h, Load_fc.cpp,
   Load_mo3.cpp, MPEGFrame.cpp) and per-format quirks.
   https://github.com/OpenMPT/openmpt

2. libxmp — MIT
   Copyright (C) 1996-2026 Claudio Matsuoka and Hipolito Carraro Jr
   Ported from: src/mixer.c, src/mix_all.c, src/effects.c, src/player.c,
   src/read_event.c, src/flow.c, src/lfo.c, src/filter.c, src/virtual.c,
   src/scan.c, src/load.c, src/loaders/*.c, src/load_helpers.c,
   src/common.h, src/include/xmp.h.
   https://github.com/libxmp/libxmp

3. Paula-Tracker — MIT
   Copyright (C) 2025 Michael Binder
   Ported from: paulalib/audio-engine.js (Paula mixing kernel).
   https://github.com/RednibCoding/Paula-Tracker

4. cRSID (libcRSID 1.58) — WTF (public-domain style; author requests attribution)
   Copyright (C) 2025-2026 Mihály Horváth (Hermit)
   Ported from: libcRSID/ — 6510 CPU, SID chip, CIA/VIC, memory banking,
   PSID/RSID loader. All tables (combined waveforms, filter curves, Sinc
   window, ADSR DAC) are verbatim copies.
   https://csdb.dk/release/?id=261057

5. stb_vorbis — dual MIT / public domain (public-domain alternative used)
   Original version written by Sean Barrett (nothings) in 2007
   Ported from: stb_vorbis.c (decoder verified bit-exact against the C build).
   https://github.com/nothings/stb

6. minimp3 — public domain (CC0 dedication)
   By lieff
   Ported from: minimp3.h (Layer-III decoder used by fmt-mo3 for
   MP3-compressed samples).
   https://github.com/lieff/minimp3

7. TinySoundFont — MIT (tsf.h) and zlib (tml.h)
   tsf.h: Copyright (C) 2017-2025 Bernhard Schelling, based on SFZero,
   Copyright (C) 2012 Steve Folta
   tml.h: Copyright (C) 2017, 2018, 2020 Bernhard Schelling
   Ported from: tsf.h (SoundFont2 synthesizer) and tml.h (TinyMidiLoader
   SMF parser), used by fmt-mid.
   https://github.com/schellingb/TinySoundFont

